**Convention 7.3 (fixed-tree common extensions).** In
[FixedTreeCommonExtension][FCE], `Full` requires disjoint sibling leaf
coordinate sets, `Implementation.encode` receives the leaf coordinate
itself, and `Implementation.combine` receives the full child-message
tuple. The public `result` assumes finite nonempty coordinate alphabets,
a fixed full tree covering those coordinates, an arbitrary nonempty
promise and a task on it. The promise may be correlated. It compares
the upward closures of reachable-message and common-total-extension
capacity vectors, with attained equal minima for monotone costs.
Its canonical implementation uses representative choice; its root
`read` is an output decoder. The [owning narrative][FCEB] has the same
scope. None of those inputs is the charged literal acquisition of
Assumption 1.3.

Theorem 3.2 supplies an original-task interface requirement for a
purported compiler from such freely supplied coordinates: on the
actual perfect-scaffold witness it must pay at least $2^{D-2}$
preparation Reads. In particular no compiler can serve all depths
with worst paid preparation $o(2^D)$ under this unchanged task and
without other acquired source data. This excludes that explicit budget
class only. Exponential preparation is permitted in the original
objective, so the bound disproves neither original feasibility nor
effective optimizer-cofinal certification.

